  "caption": "Figure 1: Gradient estimation accuracy and computation cost in VAE on MNIST. Left and middle: average (per parameter) squared bias and variance of gradient estimators versus temperature. STGS and all GR estimators share the same bias according to the theory but differ in variance. ZGR achieves the lowest bias of this family and has variance lower than GR and GS estimators for any temperature < 0.1 and substantially lower than that of unbiased ARSM. GS estimator is asymptotically unbiased but its variance grows asymptotically as O(1/τ). Right: time of a forward-backward pass on GPU. GS and GS-ST estimators are built-in in pytorch while other estimators are implemented by us in pytorch. ZGR is significantly faster than GR-MC variants and ARSM. Note that the network has only a single layer with 16 8-way categorical variables.",
